// The four-wide tree over triangles: what Embree's BVH4 and FCPW's four-wide
// Mbvh both are, before either gives it bytes. An interior node holds four
// children as one array with one box annotation over them, `AABB(lo, hi) on
// children` -- the node bounds its children, not itself, as Embree's
// AABBNode and FCPW's MbvhNode both do -- so a traversal tests the four at
// the node (Lower/Trees.cpp, from_children), which a schedule vectorizes
// into one four-wide test. A leaf holds a run of triangles.
//
// The bytes are a layout's: schedules/layouts/embree4.bonsai (Embree's
// AABBNode<4> rows and Triangle4 blocks in one arena, reached by address),
// schedules/layouts/fcpw4w16.bonsai and fcpw4w8.bonsai (FCPW's MbvhNode
// rows and packets of sixteen or eight, reached by index). Each imports
// this file; the schedules import a layout.

schedule {
    tree[[Triangle]] BVH4 =
    | Interior(children : array[BVH4, 4], lo hi : vector[vec3f, 4])
        with AABB(lo, hi) on children
    | Leaf(data : array[Triangle]) with data = data;

    triangles : BVH4;
}
